 @tonyv1796  my experience with the 5060 has been amazing compared to the 4060 
I run Minecraft at 120 fps with photon shaders, max render distance, HD textures and distant horizons at 60% GPU utilization 
While my friend with the same RAM and better CPU but with a RTX 4060 runs the same shaders at 60 fps 96% GPU utilization (no distant horizons even)

 @KrappaU  compatibility - not all gpu users are gamers.
As an example go to 8:06 and look at the Blender scores. All the top scoring cards are RTX cards. RTX cards have RT cores and RT cores work great for optix rendering. A GTX card like a 1060 can render using optix. But it would be faster to use cuda, which they didn't even test. Programs like Blender have been optimized for RTX cards. AMD cards are just okay in Blender, even high end AMD cards and it's the same for the intel arc cards.

I still have two RTX 2060 Supers in one of my rendering machines and while they are 5 years old and a bit dated, I still use them because they have 100% compatibility, they have RT cores and work great in Optix and they perform better in Blender than an AMD 9060 XT. The 5050 will smoke the 2060 super in Blender.
